  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Divaricataester C appears to interact with CX-1 through a series of molecular targets that are all involved in sialylation pathways. The evidence suggests that Divaricataester C acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, which in turn target CX-1. This implies a potential mechanism where Divaricataester C may influence the activity of these sialylation enzymes, which are critical for cellular processes such as cell surface glycosylation and signaling. The shared involvement of these targets in sialylation pathways suggests a possible functional link between Divaricataester C and CX-1, possibly through modulation of sialylation-related processes. The evidence supports a pathway where Divaricataester C may act as a modulator of sialylation enzymes, which in turn affect CX-1, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
